1000 Functional Connectomes Project (FCON1000)
==============================================

Resting-state fMRI and T1-weighted images of ~1300 participants (mostly
healthy) acquired at 33 sites, released in 2009-2010 by the 1000
Functional Connectomes Project (INDI).

    Biswal BB, Mennes M, Zuo X-N, et al. (2010) Toward discovery
    science of human brain function. PNAS 107(10):4734-4739.
    https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0911855107

Data use follows the terms of the FCON1000 release (non-commercial use;
see the INDI website). Acknowledge the contributing sites.

Organisation
------------
This dataset was assembled by brainspresso from the per-site folders of
s3://fcp-indi/data/Projects/FCON1000/:

* Subject labels are only unique within a site, so they are prefixed
  with a site code: `AnnArbor_a/sub-04111` -> `sub-AnnArborA04111`.
  `participants.tsv` lists the site and the original label.
* Several resting-state runs (`func`, `func_2`... in the source)
  become `run-1`, `run-2`... (ICBM, NewHaven_a, NewHaven_b).
  NYU_TRT has three sessions (`ses-1` to `ses-3`).
* Files were matched by folder, so typos in the source file names
  (`tast-rest`, `test-rest`, `_boldt`, `T1wnii.gz`...) are corrected.
* Repetition times were read from the NIfTI headers (most common value
  per site; 7 Atlanta subjects have TR = 2.0 s instead of 2.02 s).
* Skull-stripped T1w images are in `derivatives/fcon1000`. NewHaven_a
  and NewHaven_b only have skull-stripped anatomical images.
* Site notes and extra tables are kept in `sourcedata/<site>/`.
* `participants.tsv` merges the site tables (`handed` -> `handedness`,
  sex as M/F, `9999` -> n/a). The NewYork_a table has 4 column names
  for 5 columns: the 4th column (7.88 to 49.16) is taken to be the
  age. Several sites have no demographics.

