Notes from the sites
--------------------
* AnnArbor_a: no resting-state scan for sub-47191 and sub-56686; no
  demographic data available.
* Beijing_Zang: the resting-state scan of sub-62966 seems to be acquired
  in a different orientation. sub-26713, sub-49782, sub-66889, sub-82714
  and sub-85818 were excluded from the group analyses in the paper.
* Berlin_Margulies: resting-state scans acquired without fat suppression.
* ICBM: two ambidextrous subjects (labelled A); three resting-state
  scans per subject.
* Leiden_2180, Leiden_2200: same magnet.
* Leipzig: some T1w images are missing, because defacing failed.
* Milwaukee_a, Milwaukee_b: same magnet; no demographics for Milwaukee_a.
* Munchen: the first 5 time points of sub-70942 were not removed (fewer
  time points than the other subjects).
* NewHaven_a: sub-64608 was excluded from the analyses in the paper (no
  high-resolution anatomical image).
* NewHaven_b: not included in the analyses of the paper; four
  resting-state scans per subject (sub-47998 has three).
* NewYork_a, NewYork_a_ADHD, NewYork_b: same magnet; NewYork_a and
  NewYork_a_ADHD use the same sequence.
* Newark: the anatomical scan of sub-71042 seems stretched at the top of
  the brain.
* Ontario: 4T magnet; no anatomical scan for sub-71760 and sub-75684;
  no demographics.
* Orangeburg: 1.5T magnet.
* Queensland: the first 5 time points of sub-68733 were not removed;
  this subject was excluded from the analyses in the paper.
* Taipei_a, Taipei_b: same magnet (295 and 175 volumes respectively); no
  resting-state scan for Taipei_a sub-45138; no demographics.

Labels in these notes are the original (site) labels.
